<BlogPost slug="iptv-cost-canada">
  <p>Prices differ between providers, so the most useful number is your <strong>cost per month</strong> for the screens you actually use. Here is how that works with Prime IPTV.</p>

  <h2>Prime IPTV plan prices</h2>
  <p>With 1 connection, the published plans are:</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Price</th><th>Per month</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>3 months</td><td>$34.99</td><td>$11.66</td></tr>
        <tr><td>6 months (+1 free)</td><td>$49.99</td><td>$8.33 over 6 paid months</td></tr>
        <tr><td>12 months (+1 free)</td><td>$79.99</td><td>$6.67 over 12 paid months</td></tr>
        <tr><td>24 months (+2 free)</td><td>$124.99</td><td>$5.21 over 24 paid months</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Plans for 2, 3 and 4 connections are on the <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a>. The longer the plan, the lower the monthly cost.</p>

  <h2>Cheap does not have to mean risky</h2>
  <p>A low price is only a good deal if the service works on your connection and your must-have channels are included. Use the <a href="/free-trial/">24-hour free trial</a> before you pick a long plan, and check the <a href="/refund/">refund policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>What to include when you compare with cable</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The monthly package price, plus taxes.</li>
    <li>Box or equipment rental, and extra boxes for more TVs.</li>
    <li>Any term agreement or cancellation fee.</li>
    <li>Add-on channel and sports packages.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Your own bill is the right comparison, since cable pricing varies by provider and region.</p>

  <h2>Quick answers</h2>
  <h3>Which plan is the best value?</h3>
  <p>The 24-month plan has the lowest monthly cost, and the 12-month plan is the most popular middle choice.</p>
  <h3>Are there hidden fees?</h3>
  <p>The plan price is the price you see. Ask us on WhatsApp if you want it confirmed before you order.</p>
</BlogPost>
